<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      Tube BFF schema (the may-use GOVERNANCE plane). Liquibase runs over a JDBC
      datasource (Liquibase has no R2DBC runner); all runtime data access goes through
      R2DBC.

        004 — tube_access   (PR2 — the use grant/timeout/ban OVERLAY; desired-state
              CLONED from the owncast-bff owncast_grant (004) overlay — itself cloned from
              the wiki-bff wiki_access (004) — swapping broadcast->use: state active->revoked
              never deleted=audit, expires_at NULL=permanent / future=timeout-auto-restore,
              partial-unique on active(domain,user_subject,access_type), domain-scoped. The
              TubeAccessGuard DEFAULT-DENY enforcement reads this at request time.)

        005 — tube_google_link  (PR3 — the per-(brand,user) Google OAuth youtube.readonly
              connection. The crown-jewel REFRESH TOKEN is stored ONLY as an AES-256-GCM
              ciphertext (refresh_token_ciphertext = base64(iv||ct||tag); no plaintext
              column), encrypted by TokenCipher with the per-service DEK from ESO
              secret/<brand>/tube-token-dek. owner+domain stamped server-side; partial
              UNIQUE on the LIVE row (revoked_at IS NULL); reauth_required STOPS the sync
              loop on a refresh failure; soft-revoke = audit.)

        006 — tube_subscription (PR3 — the per-(brand,user) mirror of the user's subscribed
              YouTube channels; SubscriptionsSyncService pages subscriptions.list?mine=true
              and idempotently UPSERTs one row per channel. UNIQUE(domain,user_subject,
              channel_id).)

      The tube_download_job work queue + tube_storage_usage budgets (PR4) are added in
      later changesets. The changeSet numbering starts at 004 to match the owncast_grant
      / wiki_access (004) overlay this is cloned from (001-003 in wiki-bff are the wiki
      content store, which tube has no analogue of — use is grant-only).
    -->

    <include file="db/changelog/004-tube-access.xml"/>
    <include file="db/changelog/005-tube-google-link.xml"/>
    <include file="db/changelog/006-tube-subscription.xml"/>
</databaseChangeLog>
